vided, extract the node id and file key from the URL, for example, if given the URL https://figma.com/design/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=1-2, the extracted nodeId would be `1:2` and the fileKey would be `:fileKey`. If the URL does not include `node-id`, ask the user for a node-specific URL. Do not pass an empty or guessed nodeId. "+v+" "+(t?"If the URL is of the format https://figma.com/make/:makeFileKey/:makeFileName then use the makeFileKey to identify the Figma Make file. ":"")+"Only for Figma Make files (URLs containing `/make/`), and only when calling get_design_context, assume the nodeId is `0:1`. The response will contain a code string and a JSON of download URLs for the assets referenced in the code."+(n?" It will also include a screenshot of the node for context by default.":"")+r:x+E+" "+v+(n?" It will also include a screenshot of the node for context by default.":"")+r}function T({isRemote:e}){return e?"Generate UI code for a given FigJam node in Figma. Use the nodeId parameter to specify a node id. If no node id is provided, use `0:1` which is the root node ID. Use the fileKey parameter to specify the file key. If a URL is provided, extract the node id from the URL, for example, if given the URL https://figma.com/board/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=1-2, the extracted nodeId would be `1:2` and the fileKey would be `:fileKey`. IMPORTANT: This tool only works for FigJam files (URL path `/board/`), not other Figma files.":"Generate UI code for a given FigJam node or the currently selected FigJam node in the Figma desktop app. Use the nodeId parameter to specify a node id. If no node id is provided, the currently selected node will be used. If a URL is provided, extract the node id from the URL, for example, if given the URL https://figma.com/board/:fileKey/:fileName?node-id=1-2, the extracted nodeId would be `1:2`. IMPORTANT: This tool only works for FigJam files (URL path `/board/`), not other Figma files."}T({isRemote:!1}),!function({includePlaywrightInstruction:e,includeHtmlToFigmaGuidance:t}){}({includePlaywrightInstruction:!0,includeHtmlToFigmaGuidance:!1});function w(e){let t=!0===e.fileBrowserReadOnly;return(t?"Read an existing Figma file with JavaScript and the Figma Plugin API.\n\n**This tool is read-only in the file browser.** Use it only to inspect nodes and properties or capture screenshots. Never create, change, rename, move, or delete nodes or other file contents. When the user asks to edit a file, start its in-file agent with `seed_thread_for_file` instead.\n":!0===e.readOnlyLead?"Read the Figma scene graph with the Plugin API.\n\n**This tool reads; it does not design.** Visual changes go to `edit_design`, however small. Write here only for what it cannot do.\n":"Execute JavaScript with Figma Plugin API access. Best for precise, verifiable changes and inspecting node properties.\n")+"\n"+(!0===e.conditionalTypingsLookup?"Plugin API typings are available at `${ACTIVE_WORKSPACE}/docs/evaluate_script/figma-plugin-api.d.ts`. Grep them when an API name, signature, property, or enum is unclear, or after a related error. Do not preflight routine calls when the API is already clear from the tool schema and current context.\n":"**Before writing, grep the Plugin API typings (`${ACTIVE_WORKSPACE}/docs/evaluate_script/figma-plugin-api.d.ts`) for the exact `figma.*` signatures, properties, and enums you will use \u2014 a wrong name fails the whole call.**\n")+"Each call runs in a fresh scope \u2014 re-fetch nodes by id; nothing persists between calls.\n\n**Parameters:** name the code argument `code`, never `script` (else validation fails).\n\n**Critical \u2014 these crash or silently fail otherwise:**\n- Top-level `await`/`return` work \u2014 do NOT wrap code in an async IIFE. MUST `await` every async call (unawaited ones fail silently and time out).\n- Look up nodes with `await figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)` (null if stale) \u2014 not the sync `figma.getNodeById`.\n"+(t?"":"- Load fonts before any text edit: `await figma.loadFontAsync(node.fontName)`.\n")+"- Follow the current editor guidance for node traversal and inspection. Do not assume node-specific properties such as `children`, `layoutMode`, fills, or effects exist on every node.\n- JavaScript runtime, no TypeScript syntax. `figma.notify()` is a no-op; `figma.viewport.bounds`/`.zoom` throw \u2014 to place elements in the user's view, use the Viewport bounds from the user message. `currentPage`/selection are yours, not the user's \u2014 switch with `await figma.setCurrentPageAsync(page)`.\n"+(t?"- Reads only the file identified by the fileKey passed, load `read-file-context` first before using.\n":"- Writes target current file only. To read another accessible file, load `read-file-context` first, then pass its fileKey.\n")+"\n**Output:** `return <value>` and `console.log()` are captured; uncaught errors propagate. "+(!0===e.discourageStringify?"Return values should be JSON data types, do not stringify them. Avoid including indentation when stringifying console output. ":"")+"To verify visuals, call `await node.screenshot()` \u2014 it returns nothing and attaches a PNG of the node inline. Output is truncated if large.\n\n**Limitations:** no network/`fetch()`; no `figma.showUI()`.\n"}w({}),w({fileBrowserReadOnly:!0}),w({discourageStringify:!0}),w({readOnlyLead:!0}),w({conditionalTypingsLookup:!0});let C="get_code_for_selection",k="create_design_system_rules",R="map_selection_to_code_connect",P="Prompt to generate code for the currently selected design elements in Figma",N="Provides a prompt to generate design system rules for this repo.",O="Provides a prompt to map the currently selected design elements in Figma to code components in the codebase using Code Connect.";function D({exposeAssetWriteDirectoryOption:e,exposeScreenshotOption:t}){return{name:s,description:S({isRemote:!1,includeMakeInstruction:!1,includeScreenshotHint:t}),annotations:{readOnlyHint:!0},inputSchema:a((0,r.lz8)({exposeAssetWriteDirectoryOption:e,exposeScreen